{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455744-lost-boy-characters","id":1455744,"title":"Lost Boy Characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-28T23:14:20-07:00","id":1455744,"title":"Lost Boy Characters","content":"If we get a new 2e Grimm Fear changeling book, I would love to see Changelings trapped in eternal childhood given as potential antagonists or allies. Rather than representing the joys of eternal innocence and happiness, I can see such characters becoming bitter and sociopathic like Gertrude from <b><i>I Hate Fairyland</i></b>. Think of the horror of having to go through 3rd grade over and over again<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Plus, there is the difficulty of finding sources of income to pay for food and board and people will notice that you obviously do not age. This will force <i>Lost Boys and Lost Girls </i> to constantly have to move.<br /> <br /> I also think they would make interesting loyalists and racketeers. I can see some Lost Boys/Girls worshipping the True Fae al a <i><b>Children of the Corn </b></i>or acting like Henry Bowers gang from Stephen King's <i><b>It.</b></i><br /> <br /> They could also be interesting characters to play as. You could draw on the Loser gang from <i><b>It </b></i>for inspiration or some of the Holly Black books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T17:19:38-07:00","id":1455769,"title":"","content":"Tessie has mentioned that he made a kith based on the idea of a changeling having the appearance of a child. I have always envisioned this as a merit, which I am introducing below. I am curious to hear people's thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Lost Boy/Lost Girl</i></b><br /> <br /> Your Keeper blessed/cursed you with eternal childhood or you made a vow to never grow up with the hedge/wyrd. You are immune to the effects/penalties of aging. However, while you do not age on the outside, you age every minute on the inside. Often making <i>The Lost Boy </i>old, bitter, and sociopathic on the inside.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Other Drawbacks: </i></b>You suffer all the penalties of the petite frame. Also, because you obviously do not age, you constantly have to move. Your youthful appearance makes it difficult for you to find income for food and board.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T19:48:07-07:00","id":1455778,"title":"","content":"More thoughts, I think a <i>Lost Boy</i> who had a motley or family could have an easier resisting giving into bitterness and going down a dark path. Especially if that motley included other <i>Lost Boys.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T15:21:19-07:00","id":1455819,"title":"","content":"I have been thinking about how I would faeify some of the characters from the Lost Boys and Girl inspiration material.<br /> <br /> Fran Brow I would make either a fairest moonborn or elemental dryad (because she spends the third chapter in a form of a tree).<br /> Gertrude I would make an ogre blood brute.<br /> <br /> Mono would be a Wizened True Friend and Six would be a darkling leechfinger.<br /> <br /> But I am not sure what I would make Nick from Gerald Brom's <i>Child Thief</i>. Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T11:57:44-07:00","id":1456444,"title":"","content":"I have made some edits to the <i><b>Lost Boy </b>merit </i> and am curious to hear peoples thoughts. Based on the references I have shared, do you guys have any suggestions? Note: I decided it should be a merit, instead of a kith to give players more flexibility in the type of character they build.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Lost Boy(</i></b><b><i>\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Effect: </i></b>Your Keeper has blessed/cursed you with eternal childhood, making you immune to the effects/penalties of aging. You will never grow old and die. However, while you do not age on the outside, you age every minute on the inside. Worse, they not only STILL gain adult responsibilities like finding food, shelter, and clothing, they gain none of the benefits of adulthood, like falling in love and raising a family. This often makes the changeling bitter and mean.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Drawback: </i></b>Your characters suffers the penalties of the petit frame flaw. Also, because you so obviously do not age, Lost Boys often have to move to different regions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T16:35:53-07:00","id":1456470,"title":"","content":"Not sure if \u201cdoes not age\u201d is by itself worth a two-dot Merit. Maybe some other Social or supernatural bonuses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T18:24:58-07:00","id":1456482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455744-lost-boy-characters?p=1456470#post1456470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if \u201cdoes not age\u201d is by itself worth a two-dot Merit. Maybe some other Social or supernatural bonuses?</div> </div> </div> </div>any suggestions? I am actually thinking this might be a flaw, rather than a merit.<br /> <br /> One of the themes I am trying to portray through this flaw/merit is the difficulties of staying eternally young. Such as how does the changeling pay for food and rent? Having the appearance of a child means most businesses will give the changeling important positions with a high paying salary. For that matter, child labor laws prevent legal businesses from hiring the changeling. Plus, after a while people are going to notice that you don\u2019t age, forcing the childlike changeling to move. This makes it difficult for the changeling to form long lasting relationships. Finally, there are the predators, child molesters, pimps, and gang members who will see the changeling as easy prey. Having to deal and resolve these issues forces the character to realize that you can\u2019t remain a child forever, no matter your childlike appearance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T18:50:23-07:00","id":1456485,"title":"","content":"But Flaws aren\u2019t a thing in 2E, right? We only have Merits with natural drawbacks, and some persistent Conditions. The more \u2018realistic\u2019 hazards of being a kid feels like something more for narratives rather than mechanics, unless we\u2019re specifically talking about Social dice rolls. <br /> <br /> Iirc there have been fan attempts to update Innocents (1e general supplement) to 2e. Those, and the original book too, could be inspirations.<br /> <br /> Personally, maybe something like\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Lost in Youth (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Whether you were taken as a child and stuck there, or had enchanted youth imposed on you, your Durance has left you an eternal child. Your lifespan is still fixed, but you will not age. You are immune to penalties from old age and infirmity, and to supernatural powers that age you or make you even younger. Once per chapter, you may spend a Glamour point to either raise your Impression level in Social Maneuvering, or momentarily slip away from accusations of crimes or of a social faux pas.<br /> <b>Drawbacks</b>: To those unaware of your actual age (and even to some who are), you are fully exposed to exploitative, belittling, regulating, and patronizing perspectives.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, maybe that\u2019s now a bit too much for a two-dot? Adjustments may be needed\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 08-09-2021, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T19:02:51-07:00","id":1456487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455744-lost-boy-characters?p=1456485#post1456485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Flaws aren\u2019t a thing in 2E, right? We only have Merits with natural drawbacks, and some persistent Conditions. The more \u2018realistic\u2019 hazards of being a kid feels like something more for narratives rather than mechanics, unless we\u2019re specifically talking about Social dice rolls.<br /> <br /> Iirc there have been fan attempts to update Innocents (1e general supplement) to 2e. Those, and the original book too, could be inspirations.<br /> <br /> Personally, maybe something like\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Lost in Youth (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Whether you were taken as a child and stuck there, or had enchanted youth imposed on you, your Durance has left you an eternal child. Your lifespan is still fixed, but you will not age. You are immune to penalties from old age and infirmity, and to supernatural powers that age you or make you even younger. Once per chapter, you may spend a Glamour point to either raise your Impression level in Social Maneuvering, or momentarily slip away from accusations of crimes or of a social faux pas.<br /> <b>Drawbacks</b>: To those unaware of your actual age (and even to some who are), you are fully exposed to exploitative, belittling, regulating, and patronizing perspectives.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, maybe that\u2019s now a bit too much for a two-dot? Adjustments may be needed\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>In general I like this, though the way I envision it, the character will not die of old age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T19:31:48-07:00","id":1456489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455744-lost-boy-characters?p=1456487#post1456487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general I like this, though the way I envision it, the character will not die of old age.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my original idea too, though I backed away from it only because immortality\u2019s rather distant in the CofD in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T19:59:16-07:00","id":1456491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455744-lost-boy-characters?p=1456489#post1456489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was my original idea too, though I backed away from it only because immortality\u2019s rather distant in the CofD in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think it is possible to play such a character. For one thing, Vampire: The Requiem has introduced Vampire methuselahs who are more than two thousand years old in <b><i>Thousand Years of Night. </i></b>Plus, the 2e changeling corebook talks about ageless fae, which suggests we might meet Changeling characters who are immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T20:11:16-07:00","id":1456492,"title":"","content":"Forgot to give some examples,<br /> <br /> Ann Harlow, a Daeva who has been a vampire for more than 2,350 years.<br /> Ezekiel of Sodom from the Akhud, who is more than a thousand years old.<br /> And the survivors of the Julii; Priscus and Patrizia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T17:17:26-07:00","id":1456566,"title":"","content":"I took some of 21C Hermits advice for the edits to the <i>Lost Boy</i> merit, though I kept that the character will not die of old age. I am curious to hear people's thoughts. On one hand, I am afraid that the merits immunity to supernatural effects that cause decrepitude might be too powerful, because it makes them immune to many spells that deal with death. This is why the Lost Boy is not immune to spells that cause sickness.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Lost Boy(</i></b><b><i>\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b><i>Effect: </i></b>Your Keeper has blessed/cursed you with eternal childhood, making you immune to the effects/penalties of aging, as well as any supernatural power that effects aging and decrepitude. You can still be affected by mundane and supernatural forms of disease. Once per chapter, you can spend a point of glamor and raise your social impression by your wyrd level to emotionally coerce a character through your innocent appearance. Other changelings can make a composure+ wyrd roll to try to resist this affect.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Drawback: </i></b>Because of your appearance, you look like easy prey to child molesters, pimps, and gang members. Also, because you so obviously do not age, Lost Boys often have to move to different regions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T20:15:38-07:00","id":1456573,"title":"","content":"You may also want to give Lost Boys the option of getting the Small merit for free - most are logically going to have it, and Small has drawbacks in and of itself to balance its perks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T20:33:34-07:00","id":1456575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzauri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455744-lost-boy-characters?p=1456573#post1456573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may also want to give Lost Boys the option of getting the Small merit for free - most are logically going to have it, and Small has drawbacks in and of itself to balance its perks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, for the suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T13:51:06-07:00","id":1456782,"title":"","content":"Immortality is something in faerie mythos for sure, but keep this in mind. In changeling, there are ways to become immortsl, but all of them are pretty intense. Certain Entitlements can do it. There are also likely Goblin Fruits you can use, but will then become dependent on (addiction is a strong word to use but it's not inaccurate). I'd imagine there are other factors that can cause it as well.<br /> <br /> I would honestly run the immortality and eternal youth as separate traits, but ones that a given changeling can have both of. One to represent eternal youth (and immunity to time tampering. If mummies can do it, it can work). The other representing immortality itself.<br /> <br /> That way, you can have immortal changelings and all the questions that get asked behind their back about how they did it. And you can also have a changeling who doesn't age, even if they will eventually die. And you can have a rare few who have both. That gives space for, say, tolkienesque Elves that will last as long as vampires and mummies. You can have Michael Darling and the Gump (from Legend). And because it's poorly understood IC (due to being two separate things ooc), a truly immortal child would raise lots of questions amongst mortal and fae alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T15:05:06-07:00","id":1456786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1455744-lost-boy-characters?p=1456782#post1456782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immortality is something in faerie mythos for sure, but keep this in mind. In changeling, there are ways to become immortsl, but all of them are pretty intense. Certain Entitlements can do it. There are also likely Goblin Fruits you can use, but will then become dependent on (addiction is a strong word to use but it's not inaccurate). I'd imagine there are other factors that can cause it as well.<br /> <br /> I would honestly run the immortality and eternal youth as separate traits, but ones that a given changeling can have both of. One to represent eternal youth (and immunity to time tampering. If mummies can do it, it can work). The other representing immortality itself..</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear what you are saying and agree that there are multiple ways to gain immortality in Changeling including reaching wyrd 10 and the merit <i>Long of Days</i>. I chose to include immortality in the <i><b>Lost Boy </b></i>merit, is one of the reasons Peter Pan chose to stay young forever was fear of growing old and dying. I wanted to show the consequences of immortality combined with staying a child forever.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}